#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: sea*P.*
#> pause: 45
#> must: # command:  sed -n -f
#> must: A stately pleasure dome decree*P:*
#> must: Where Alph*P,* the sacred river*P,* ran
#> must: Down to a sunless sea*P.*
#> not: In Xanadu
#> not: measureless
#> source: *P&*
# 11. & in the replacement, and the p flag. McMahon 3.2
# [.,;?:] matches one punctuation character. In the replacement, & stands for
# whatever the pattern matched, so each mark becomes *P<mark>*. The g flag
# does it for every match on the line; the p flag prints the line only if a
# substitution happened, which with -n means only the punctuated lines show.
# Try: drop the g: only the first mark on each line is wrapped.
#ARGS -n
s/[.,;?:]/*P&*/gp

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
